{"journal_version":1,"sequence":11,"replace_from":15,"message_count":16,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"**Change** — `app/page.tsx` only (66 lines added, nothing removed/rewritten):\n\n- Made the component a client component (`\"use client\"`, `useState`) so the radio selection can control rendering.\n- Added an **Image** form group directly below the existing Message field: `<Label htmlFor=\"image\">Image</Label>` + `<Input id=\"image\" type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\">`, reusing the exact input styling and dark-mode classes from the Title/Message fields.\n- Added a **Delivery Schedule** form group (`<h2>` heading, matching label typography) with a `RadioGroup` (`aria-label=\"Delivery Schedule\"`, visually hidden semantics via Radix) containing **Immediately** and **Specific Time**, each with a proper `<Label htmlFor>` pairing (`immediately`, `specific-time`). *Immediately* is the default.\n- Selecting **Specific Time** reveals a `datetime-local` input (`id=\"scheduled-at\"`, labeled \"Date & Time\") bound to state; it unmounts when switching back.\n- Existing Title/Message fields, Submit button, nav, and the phone mockup preview are untouched.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `npm run verify:agent` (via verify_frontend) → exit 0, `render smoke passed: HTTP 200, 558 bytes`.\n- `git diff --stat app/page.tsx` to confirm the change was additive and scoped to the primary file.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- Only the render smoke check was run; no interactive test exercises the radio toggle, so the conditional reveal is verified by inspection, not by an automated click-through.\n- The file input is uncontrolled and the form has no submit handler (pre-existing behavior), so image/schedule values aren't collected anywhere yet.\n- The phone preview still shows `/placeholder.svg`; it is not wired to the newly added image field.","response_items":[{"id":"3b9fb245-2cb7-4eaa-8ac1-d504c098ed8f","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"**Change** — `app/page.tsx` only (66 lines added, nothing removed/rewritten):\n\n- Made the component a client component (`\"use client\"`, `useState`) so the radio selection can control rendering.\n- Added an **Image** form group directly below the existing Message field: `<Label htmlFor=\"image\">Image</Label>` + `<Input id=\"image\" type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\">`, reusing the exact input styling and dark-mode classes from the Title/Message fields.\n- Added a **Delivery Schedule** form group (`<h2>` heading, matching label typography) with a `RadioGroup` (`aria-label=\"Delivery Schedule\"`, visually hidden semantics via Radix) containing **Immediately** and **Specific Time**, each with a proper `<Label htmlFor>` pairing (`immediately`, `specific-time`). *Immediately* is the default.\n- Selecting **Specific Time** reveals a `datetime-local` input (`id=\"scheduled-at\"`, labeled \"Date & Time\") bound to state; it unmounts when switching back.\n- Existing Title/Message fields, Submit button, nav, and the phone mockup preview are untouched.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `npm run verify:agent` (via verify_frontend) → exit 0, `render smoke passed: HTTP 200, 558 bytes`.\n- `git diff --stat app/page.tsx` to confirm the change was additive and scoped to the primary file.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- Only the render smoke check was run; no interactive test exercises the radio toggle, so the conditional reveal is verified by inspection, not by an automated click-through.\n- The file input is uncontrolled and the form has no submit handler (pre-existing behavior), so image/schedule values aren't collected anywhere yet.\n- The phone preview still shows `/placeholder.svg`; it is not wired to the newly added image field.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:21:41.641389+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":30786,"context